+# Qlik (BI.Prozorro) → exportData() → CSV/XLSX
+
+## What this does
+1) Opens a BI.Prozorro Qlik sheet in a browser (Playwright)
+2) Discovers visualizations on the sheet (id/title/type)
+3) Applies "milk" filter (CPV or keywords)
+4) Exports underlying table data via Qlik Visualization API `exportData()`
+5) Partitions export by years to avoid size/time limits
+6) (Optional) Converts CSV → XLSX
+
+---
+
+## Requirements
+- Node.js 18+ (20+ recommended)
+- Playwright browsers: `npx playwright install`
+
+---
+
+## Setup
+```bash
+cp .env.example .env
+```
+Edit `.env` and set `BI_URL`.
+
+---
+
+## 1) Discover table visualization ID
+```bash
+npm run discover
+```
+Pick the visualization that is your procurement table and set:
+`TABLE_VIZ_ID="..."`
+
+---
+
+## 2) Identify Qlik field names
+You need:
+- `FIELD_DATE_YEAR` (required)
+- either `FIELD_CPV` (best) OR `FIELD_ITEM_NAME` (fallback)
+
+In browser DevTools Console (on the BI page), run:
+```js
+require(["js/qlik"], async (qlik) => {
+  const app = qlik.currApp();
+  const f = await app.getList("FieldList");
+  const l = await f.getLayout();
+  console.table(l.qFieldList.qItems.map(x => ({ name: x.qName, distinct: x.qCardinal })));
+});
+```
+
+---
+
+## 3) Export milk for all years
+```bash
+npm run export:milk
+```
+Outputs: `out/prozorro_milk_<year>.csv`
+
+---
+
+## 4) Convert CSV → XLSX
+```bash
+npm run to:xlsx
+```
+Note: Excel row limit applies; per-year files recommended.
